# EEI6373 Performance Modelling Mini Project

This branch contains the supporting materials for the EEI6373 Performance
Modelling mini project based on the Webhook Delivery System.

## Study

The study evaluates the performance of the webhook delivery system under
increasing workload and different worker configurations.

The performance model focuses on the queue and worker-processing path:

Incoming Webhook Events → Redis/RQ Queue → RQ Workers → Target Webhook

## Dataset

The dataset was generated using a controlled discrete-event simulation.

The simulation records:

- Arrival rate
- Number of workers
- Processing latency
- Throughput
- Mean queue length
- Worker utilization

The dataset contains simulation results and is not presented as production
measurements from the deployed Project 9 system.

## Experiments

1. Increasing workload with one worker
2. Increasing the number of workers at a fixed workload
3. Increasing workload and worker capacity together
